{{Setting|'''Use&amp;amp;nbsp;bounding&amp;amp;nbsp;polygons'''|Specifies whether the bounding polygon optimization is enabled for the icon. This setting reduces the number of pixels covered by the icon by using a tight polygon with 3&amp;amp;ndash;6 sides instead of a quad. This has no effect on the visual appearance of an icon, but it can increase performance for icons rendered at large sizes. This can have a ''negative'' effect on performance when icons are rendered at small sizes, so it should not be enabled in those cases.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Setting|'''Use&amp;amp;nbsp;rectangle&amp;amp;nbsp;optimization'''|Specifies that the icon is to be rendered as a rectangle primitive, if supported by the hardware. This optimization should be enabled only for an icon that is known to always be rendered aligned to the screen axes.}}&lt;br /&gt;
